৬৪. To make a 550-gram cake, if twice as much flour as sugar and $1\frac{1}{2}$ times as much sugar as raisins are needed, how much flour will be needed? [Primary Headmaster (Padma) - '12]
A. 225 grams
B. 250 grams
C. 275 grams
D. **300 grams**

+++ Explanation:
Raisins : Sugar : Flour $= 1 : \frac{3}{2} : \left(\frac{3}{2} \times 2\right) = 1 : \frac{3}{2} : 3 = 2 : 3 : 6$
Sum of ratio terms $= 2 + 3 + 6 = 11$
11 parts $= 550 \text{ grams} \implies \text{Flour (6 parts)} = \frac{550 \times 6}{11} = 300 \text{ grams}$
+++

