৬৬. A box contains 50-poisha, 25-poisha, and 10-poisha coins in the ratio 1 : 2 : 5. If there is a total of 33 Taka, how much money is there in 50-poisha coins alone? [National Security Intelligence (NSI) Junior Field Officer - 2019]
A. 12 Taka
B. 15 Taka
C. **11 Taka**
D. 10 Taka

+++ Explanation:
Let number of coins be $x$, $2x$, and $5x$ respectively.
Total value in poisha $= 50(x) + 25(2x) + 10(5x) = 33 \times 100$
$50x + 50x + 50x = 3300 \implies 150x = 3300 \implies x = 22$
Number of 50-poisha coins $= 22$
$\therefore \text{Value of 50-poisha coins} = 22 \times 0.50 = 11 \text{ Taka}$
+++</md></sn>